1
00:00:01,543 --> 00:00:03,629
-[car engine revving]
-[dramatic music]

2
00:00:07,132 --> 00:00:09,218
Oh, man, let's hope this works!

3
00:00:09,218 --> 00:00:10,594
Hope what works?

4
00:00:11,845 --> 00:00:13,222
-Awesome!
-Whoo-hoo!

5
00:00:17,935 --> 00:00:20,938
Not bad for something
I didn't have any time
to test out, right?

6
00:00:20,938 --> 00:00:23,398
Sure, but a head's up
would have been nice!

7
00:00:23,398 --> 00:00:26,652
Oh did I not mention
this thing splits apart?

8
00:00:26,944 --> 00:00:28,737
-Negatory.
-Sorry.

9
00:00:28,737 --> 00:00:31,490
I mean, why'd you think we each
had our own little cockpits?

10
00:00:31,490 --> 00:00:33,033
Just thought it looked cool.

11
00:00:33,033 --> 00:00:35,827
Come on, we gotta catch
up to that Pace Dragon!

12
00:00:35,827 --> 00:00:38,080
[dramatic music continues]

13
00:00:38,080 --> 00:00:40,040
[crowd cheering]

14
00:00:40,040 --> 00:00:41,416
Yeah, baby!

15
00:00:41,416 --> 00:00:43,669
Do I put on the
sweetest games or what?

16
00:00:43,669 --> 00:00:44,711
What-what?

17
00:00:46,672 --> 00:00:51,552
The Merge was
caused by Master Wu.

18
00:00:51,552 --> 00:00:54,096
-That can't be true!
-But it is.

19
00:00:54,096 --> 00:00:58,016
The Ninja's precious Master
Wu was the very person

20
00:00:58,016 --> 00:00:59,893
who caused the Merge.

21
00:00:59,893 --> 00:01:04,439
He is solely responsible for
your parents going missing,

22
00:01:04,439 --> 00:01:07,901
and every other catastrophic
effect of the Merge.

23
00:01:07,901 --> 00:01:10,487
No way.
Master Wu was a wise man.

24
00:01:10,487 --> 00:01:12,823
He wouldn't have
caused all that.

25
00:01:12,823 --> 00:01:17,953
[chuckles] Arin, you still see
the world as a tiny child does.

26
00:01:17,953 --> 00:01:19,413
Yeah, right.

27
00:01:19,413 --> 00:01:23,292
To you, the Ninja
are always good,

28
00:01:23,292 --> 00:01:26,336
and I am always the villain.

29
00:01:26,336 --> 00:01:28,881
Okay, I agree with that.

30
00:01:28,881 --> 00:01:33,093
[sighs] Real life doesn't
work like that.

31
00:01:33,093 --> 00:01:37,723
There is light in the darkness,
and darkness in the light.

32
00:01:37,723 --> 00:01:41,643
So I'm supposed to believe
you're some kinda hero?

33
00:01:41,643 --> 00:01:45,105
I've done harsh things.

34
00:01:45,105 --> 00:01:48,817
But always in the service
of reversing the Merge.

35
00:01:48,817 --> 00:01:51,987
That's really been your
goal this whole time?

36
00:01:51,987 --> 00:01:53,697
Undoing the Merge?

37
00:01:53,697 --> 00:01:56,575
Only by re-separating
the Merged Lands

38
00:01:56,575 --> 00:01:59,870
will we be able to save
them from each other.

39
00:01:59,870 --> 00:02:02,247
It must be done.

40
00:02:02,247 --> 00:02:06,710
And the process could bring
back all of those who were lost.

41
00:02:06,710 --> 00:02:08,504
I...

42
00:02:08,504 --> 00:02:10,088
I don't trust you.

43
00:02:10,088 --> 00:02:13,800
I don't need you to
believe me now, Arin.

44
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:17,971
Because I know the day will
come when you see I am right.

45
00:02:17,971 --> 00:02:21,642
Let's hope you do
before it's too late.

46
00:02:23,060 --> 00:02:25,812
You mean, we're free to go?

47
00:02:25,812 --> 00:02:27,814
You always were.

48
00:02:30,567 --> 00:02:33,195
[Ras laughing]

49
00:02:34,571 --> 00:02:37,866
♪ Lost in the unknown
so much to see ♪

50
00:02:37,866 --> 00:02:40,285
♪ Together we will rise ♪

51
00:02:40,285 --> 00:02:43,830
♪ We fight ♪

52
00:02:43,830 --> 00:02:46,917
♪ Be a ninja for what's right ♪

53
00:02:48,502 --> 00:02:50,087
[flames whooshing]

54
00:02:50,087 --> 00:02:55,092
-[dramatic music]
-[engines revving]

55
00:02:57,678 --> 00:02:59,680
I don't see the Pace
Dragon anywhere.

56
00:03:01,557 --> 00:03:02,975
Don't lose hope.

57
00:03:02,975 --> 00:03:05,435
I need a better vantage point.

58
00:03:06,895 --> 00:03:08,939
Found it!
Is it close?

59
00:03:08,939 --> 00:03:11,358
I'd say it's the
opposite of close.

60
00:03:11,358 --> 00:03:12,943
Pour on the speed!

61
00:03:12,943 --> 00:03:16,697
[dramatic music continues]

62
00:03:19,908 --> 00:03:23,453
Ha!
Pace this, dragon!

63
00:03:30,586 --> 00:03:33,505
Come on, we can pass it
inside this tunnel...

64
00:03:33,505 --> 00:03:35,090
-Uh oh!
-What "Uh oh?"

65
00:03:35,090 --> 00:03:36,341
Don't just say "Uh oh!"

66
00:03:36,341 --> 00:03:38,760
There's been a cave-in!

67
00:03:38,760 --> 00:03:40,470
There's no other way through!

68
00:03:41,346 --> 00:03:43,348
So what are you suggesting?

69
00:03:43,348 --> 00:03:45,017
Driving right into this wall?

70
00:03:45,017 --> 00:03:47,352
-Great idea, Nya!
-What?

71
00:03:47,352 --> 00:03:48,937
[Nya] That was not an idea!

72
00:03:49,646 --> 00:03:51,523
I hope this works...

73
00:03:51,523 --> 00:03:53,984
If it doesn't, we'll
find out real quick.

74
00:03:58,030 --> 00:04:00,616
I was guessing this thing
would be strong
enough when combined.

75
00:04:00,616 --> 00:04:04,036
Master Wu did say,
"Only unity can save us."

76
00:04:04,036 --> 00:04:05,245
Do you think he
was talking about

77
00:04:05,245 --> 00:04:07,206
driving through a rock wall?

78
00:04:07,206 --> 00:04:09,750
-Probably not.
-Come on!

79
00:04:09,750 --> 00:04:11,043
We gotta beat that dragon!

80
00:04:11,043 --> 00:04:12,920
Hold onto your masks!

81
00:04:12,920 --> 00:04:15,589
[dramatic music continues]

82
00:04:17,382 --> 00:04:18,842
[all gasping]

83
00:04:23,013 --> 00:04:24,515
What the what?

84
00:04:24,515 --> 00:04:26,308
They did it!

85
00:04:26,308 --> 00:04:28,519
That was ultra stang-zoot!

86
00:04:28,519 --> 00:04:30,312
I hereby gotta say,

87
00:04:30,312 --> 00:04:34,441
the Ninja are officially
still in the games!

88
00:04:38,028 --> 00:04:40,489
[gentle music]

89
00:04:46,662 --> 00:04:48,455
Thanks, Riyu.

90
00:04:48,455 --> 00:04:49,915
I know I should talk to Lloyd,

91
00:04:50,249 --> 00:04:52,000
but he'll never
believe his Uncle Wu

92
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:54,127
could've done
something that bad.

93
00:04:54,127 --> 00:04:57,840
-[Riyu chirping]
-Yeah, Ras is probably lying.

94
00:04:57,840 --> 00:05:00,300
But what if it's
even partly true?

95
00:05:00,300 --> 00:05:03,846
Frak trusts him, and he was
always a great judge of people.

96
00:05:05,347 --> 00:05:07,558
And Ras is right
about one thing.

97
00:05:07,558 --> 00:05:10,143
I'm not the ninja I should be.

98
00:05:10,143 --> 00:05:13,355
You really think Sora
faked my object Spinjitzu

99
00:05:13,355 --> 00:05:14,940
and didn't tell me?

100
00:05:15,691 --> 00:05:19,653
Yeah. Yeah, Ras is probably
lying about that, too.

101
00:05:19,653 --> 00:05:20,696
I hope.

102
00:05:22,614 --> 00:05:24,575
[Kai] Riyu?
Can you hear me?

103
00:05:24,575 --> 00:05:28,120
-We need help.
-Hey, buddy.

104
00:05:28,120 --> 00:05:30,497
Thought we were having
a moment here, but okay.

105
00:05:30,497 --> 00:05:31,999
You do you.

106
00:05:34,376 --> 00:05:35,752
[dramatic music]

107
00:05:35,752 --> 00:05:37,588
Come on, Euphrasia...

108
00:05:41,175 --> 00:05:43,093
[yelling]

109
00:05:43,093 --> 00:05:46,305
[crowd cheering]

110
00:05:46,305 --> 00:05:48,599
-Whoa!
-Close one!

111
00:05:49,141 --> 00:05:50,684
Remember, whoever
knocks their opponent

112
00:05:50,684 --> 00:05:53,020
off their platform
first equals: winner!

113
00:05:53,020 --> 00:05:54,813
Cloud Monk!

114
00:05:54,813 --> 00:05:58,358
What do your precious
scrolls say about this match?

115
00:05:59,109 --> 00:06:02,070
The Writers of Destiny
no longer believe

116
00:06:02,070 --> 00:06:04,573
our words dictate all outcomes.

117
00:06:04,573 --> 00:06:10,871
We also use our actions
to help decide our fate!

118
00:06:10,871 --> 00:06:13,582
Well, my actions
will decide yours!

119
00:06:16,627 --> 00:06:18,212
We have a winner!

120
00:06:23,592 --> 00:06:24,968
[Zeatrix laughs]

121
00:06:24,968 --> 00:06:27,513
The Elemental Power of Wind!

122
00:06:27,513 --> 00:06:31,058
A perfect compliment
to my powers!

123
00:06:31,058 --> 00:06:33,185
See how I handled that monk?

124
00:06:33,185 --> 00:06:35,562
That's nothing
compared to the destiny

125
00:06:35,562 --> 00:06:37,147
I'm gonna write for you, Ras.

126
00:06:38,398 --> 00:06:40,234
[Ras growls]

127
00:06:40,234 --> 00:06:42,986
[dramatic music]

128
00:06:45,572 --> 00:06:50,077
Uh-oh! A cloud of knock-out gas
so thick you could chew on it!

129
00:06:50,327 --> 00:06:53,872
[dramatic music continues]

130
00:06:57,709 --> 00:06:59,169
[crowd gasps]

131
00:06:59,169 --> 00:07:02,130
Nokt wins!
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

132
00:07:02,130 --> 00:07:04,883
Security!
Stop or you're disqualified!

133
00:07:07,928 --> 00:07:09,763
[Nokt chuckles]

134
00:07:09,763 --> 00:07:13,851
Told you it would be
no problem, sister.

135
00:07:13,851 --> 00:07:15,060
Sister?

136
00:07:15,060 --> 00:07:18,689
One, two, three.
One, two, three.

137
00:07:18,689 --> 00:07:19,731
Hey Frak.

138
00:07:20,315 --> 00:07:23,402
Hey, man! Sorry I haven't
been around much,

139
00:07:23,402 --> 00:07:25,863
my Master put me on an
intense training regiment.

140
00:07:25,863 --> 00:07:27,948
I haven't even seen many games.

141
00:07:27,948 --> 00:07:31,451
Frak, why didn't you tell
me Ras was your master?

142
00:07:31,451 --> 00:07:33,120
Why? Do you know him?

143
00:07:33,120 --> 00:07:35,455
Yeah. He's an enemy
to the Ninja.

144
00:07:35,455 --> 00:07:37,457
Ras hunted dragons for Imperium,

145
00:07:37,457 --> 00:07:39,334
he captured the Cloud Kingdom-

146
00:07:39,334 --> 00:07:41,545
Uh, maybe we're talking about
different guy named Ras?

147
00:07:41,545 --> 00:07:43,839
Because he's been
nothing but good to me.

148
00:07:43,839 --> 00:07:47,050
Just tell me, have you used
one of those Wolf Masks

149
00:07:47,050 --> 00:07:48,760
with the gong?

150
00:07:48,760 --> 00:07:49,845
I wish!

151
00:07:49,845 --> 00:07:51,763
Shatterspin is amazing!

152
00:07:51,763 --> 00:07:54,683
But my Master says first I
need to get my skills up.

153
00:07:54,683 --> 00:07:55,767
That's why I've been
training so hard.

154
00:07:55,767 --> 00:07:58,187
Don't do it ever!

155
00:07:58,187 --> 00:08:01,523
The Gong actually shatters
the goodness inside you.

156
00:08:01,523 --> 00:08:03,066
You're joking, right?

157
00:08:03,066 --> 00:08:05,569
Those masks will make
you more powerful,

158
00:08:05,569 --> 00:08:07,905
but they corrupt you.
Poison you.

159
00:08:07,905 --> 00:08:12,034
Ras only cares about power,
no matter what the cost.

160
00:08:12,034 --> 00:08:14,620
That doesn't sound right.

161
00:08:14,620 --> 00:08:17,164
Everything Ras taught me
to do has built me up.

162
00:08:17,164 --> 00:08:20,167
Look, I'll show you.
Follow my movements.

163
00:08:20,167 --> 00:08:22,961
Ras says everyone
spends too much time

164
00:08:22,961 --> 00:08:24,880
trying to find harmony.

165
00:08:24,880 --> 00:08:28,717
But you can't passively wait
for the world to harmonize...

166
00:08:28,717 --> 00:08:32,179
So you must take from
life what you need.

167
00:08:32,179 --> 00:08:34,890
Well, I do feel
like sometimes life

168
00:08:34,890 --> 00:08:38,268
is just dragging me along.
Hyah!

169
00:08:38,268 --> 00:08:42,064
I've been able to do a wonky
form of Spinjitzu for a while.

170
00:08:42,064 --> 00:08:44,942
Hyah! But I haven't
progressed at all.

171
00:08:44,942 --> 00:08:49,029
My master says we must
force the progress we need.

172
00:08:49,029 --> 00:08:51,782
Force the world to work
the way you want it to.

173
00:08:53,116 --> 00:08:54,826
Power through!

174
00:08:57,162 --> 00:08:58,205
Whoa!

175
00:09:00,666 --> 00:09:02,960
I did it. I did it!

176
00:09:02,960 --> 00:09:06,505
-A real Spinjitzu tornado!
-Nice!

177
00:09:06,505 --> 00:09:09,424
You have no idea how long
I've been trying to do that!

178
00:09:09,424 --> 00:09:12,719
That felt amazing!
That felt right!

179
00:09:12,719 --> 00:09:16,640
And all it took was a little bit
of my Master Ras's teachings.

180
00:09:16,640 --> 00:09:19,184
[phone chiming]

181
00:09:19,184 --> 00:09:21,478
Speaking of which,
my Master wants me

182
00:09:21,478 --> 00:09:24,231
to come to the plaza.
Maybe I'm competing today!

183
00:09:24,231 --> 00:09:25,649
Let's go!

184
00:09:25,649 --> 00:09:27,985
[Arin sighs]

185
00:09:29,403 --> 00:09:32,155
[dramatic music]

186
00:09:36,451 --> 00:09:39,621
Lloyd looks absolutely
green with envy

187
00:09:39,621 --> 00:09:42,791
at Mr. Pale's
light-bending inviso-power!

188
00:09:45,669 --> 00:09:47,504
[grunting

189
00:09:47,504 --> 00:09:48,672
Ow!

190
00:09:48,672 --> 00:09:50,174
When did you learn to do that?

191
00:09:50,174 --> 00:09:53,343
You're not the only one
who's been training!

192
00:09:53,343 --> 00:09:57,097
We gotta lot of catching
up to do, buddy,

193
00:09:57,097 --> 00:09:59,141
after I bring home that trophy!

194
00:09:59,141 --> 00:10:01,268
Now this is just
getting annoying.

195
00:10:08,901 --> 00:10:10,903
[crowd cheering]

196
00:10:10,903 --> 00:10:14,031
It was impossible not
to see that victory!

197
00:10:14,031 --> 00:10:16,074
Lloyd wins!

198
00:10:16,074 --> 00:10:18,160
Well-played, Greenie.

199
00:10:18,160 --> 00:10:19,828
Well-played.

200
00:10:21,997 --> 00:10:24,124
Wow, since you've
always been invisible,

201
00:10:24,124 --> 00:10:26,418
I've never actually
seen your face before.

202
00:10:26,418 --> 00:10:29,463
That's an interesting beard.

203
00:10:29,463 --> 00:10:32,633
Yeah, you try shaving
with invisible skin.

204
00:10:34,384 --> 00:10:37,179
Now Lloyd has the
powers of Mr. Pale.

205
00:10:37,179 --> 00:10:40,015
Care to prove it?

206
00:10:40,015 --> 00:10:43,101
-[crowd cheering]
-Where is he?

207
00:10:43,852 --> 00:10:45,479
Zero time to chillax,

208
00:10:45,479 --> 00:10:48,607
'cause the next two
competitors are up!

209
00:10:48,607 --> 00:10:52,736
First, he's the ninja
that flirts with dirt,

210
00:10:52,736 --> 00:10:55,656
Cole, Elemental Master of Earth!

211
00:10:55,656 --> 00:10:57,449
-Huh.
-Really.

212
00:10:57,449 --> 00:11:02,955
And his competitor: The
snake who shakes and breaks!

213
00:11:02,955 --> 00:11:06,333
He's Frak, Elemental
Master of Quake!

214
00:11:06,333 --> 00:11:09,044
[crowd cheering]

215
00:11:10,921 --> 00:11:13,715
Why is Arin with him?

216
00:11:13,715 --> 00:11:15,092
Hey, Arin...

217
00:11:16,593 --> 00:11:17,970
I'm here!

218
00:11:17,970 --> 00:11:20,013
It's an honor to
compete with you, Cole!

219
00:11:20,013 --> 00:11:22,057
-Sorry I was late, Roby!
-No problem.

220
00:11:22,057 --> 00:11:25,060
No one loves a dramatic
entrance more than me!

221
00:11:25,060 --> 00:11:27,354
This event puts
the hurt in hurdle!

222
00:11:27,354 --> 00:11:30,983
To win, you gotta be the
first to ring the bell!

223
00:11:30,983 --> 00:11:34,361
You ring, you
cling onto victory.

224
00:11:34,361 --> 00:11:36,488
Stang-Zoot!

225
00:11:36,488 --> 00:11:38,115
[bell rings]

226
00:11:38,365 --> 00:11:41,034
[dramatic music]

227
00:11:41,034 --> 00:11:42,828
[grunting]

228
00:11:46,957 --> 00:11:50,043
Oh no!
Is it over for Cole?

229
00:11:50,043 --> 00:11:52,629
[dramatic music continues]

230
00:11:52,629 --> 00:11:53,839
[grunting]

231
00:12:01,513 --> 00:12:03,098
Can't control metal!

232
00:12:04,558 --> 00:12:08,145
So now you believe me that
Frak is on Ras's team?

233
00:12:08,145 --> 00:12:09,730
I told you I
wouldn't lie to you.

234
00:12:09,730 --> 00:12:11,815
-Are you sure about that?
-Huh?

235
00:12:11,815 --> 00:12:14,484
Someone told me that during
the Blood Moon Ritual,

236
00:12:14,484 --> 00:12:17,362
I didn't knock out Ras
with my object Spinjitzu.

237
00:12:18,071 --> 00:12:20,824
That you used your power
to make me think I did.

238
00:12:20,824 --> 00:12:23,368
-[crashing]
-[crowd gasping]

239
00:12:23,368 --> 00:12:25,037
I...

240
00:12:25,037 --> 00:12:26,288
I did.

241
00:12:26,288 --> 00:12:27,789
I'm sorry.

242
00:12:27,789 --> 00:12:30,167
Nya was about to be sent
into the Nether Space.

243
00:12:30,167 --> 00:12:33,420
You were our only hope and
I couldn't let you fail.

244
00:12:33,420 --> 00:12:36,715
And you were so frustrated when
you got demoted in training,

245
00:12:36,715 --> 00:12:38,634
I just wanted you to have a win.

246
00:12:38,634 --> 00:12:40,802
So not even my best friend

247
00:12:40,802 --> 00:12:42,679
thought I could do it on my own.

248
00:12:42,679 --> 00:12:45,265
No, it's not like that, I...

249
00:12:51,313 --> 00:12:56,318
It's like this whole thing
is built for Frak's powers.

250
00:12:59,071 --> 00:13:02,366
Photo finish! But this photo
has a clear winner.

251
00:13:02,366 --> 00:13:04,868
Frak is victorious!

252
00:13:04,868 --> 00:13:07,120
[laughing]
You have no idea

253
00:13:07,120 --> 00:13:09,540
how exciting it is
to have met you, Cole.

254
00:13:09,540 --> 00:13:11,708
You've always been
an inspiration to me.

255
00:13:13,585 --> 00:13:15,170
Uh, thanks?

256
00:13:17,130 --> 00:13:18,590
I can't believe it!

257
00:13:21,134 --> 00:13:22,761
It's like when I used to
pretend to be a Ninja,

258
00:13:22,761 --> 00:13:24,221
but it's a real power!

259
00:13:24,221 --> 00:13:26,265
Woo-hoo!

260
00:13:26,265 --> 00:13:28,141
You fought hard, Cole.

261
00:13:28,141 --> 00:13:29,268
You should be proud.

262
00:13:29,268 --> 00:13:31,144
Not to be that guy,

263
00:13:31,144 --> 00:13:34,189
but did this game seem
weighted against us?

264
00:13:34,189 --> 00:13:37,234
Yes. And remember how we
didn't get invitations

265
00:13:37,234 --> 00:13:38,610
in the first place?

266
00:13:38,610 --> 00:13:40,612
I'm having some suspicions.

267
00:13:42,322 --> 00:13:44,700
We have some time
before the next game,

268
00:13:44,700 --> 00:13:46,618
but we need to keep
our skills sharp.

269
00:13:46,618 --> 00:13:48,328
Every time we lose,

270
00:13:48,328 --> 00:13:51,582
Ras gets closer to whatever
his evil endgame is.

271
00:13:56,712 --> 00:13:59,798
How did you pull
out that landing?

272
00:13:59,798 --> 00:14:04,094
I've got the elemental power
of balance now, remember?

273
00:14:04,094 --> 00:14:07,097
Sora, I can tell
you're distracted.

274
00:14:07,097 --> 00:14:10,601
And if you're distracted,
you'll never achieve Spinjitzu.

275
00:14:10,601 --> 00:14:14,855
I know, I know. I just, have a
lot on my mind right now.

276
00:14:14,855 --> 00:14:17,774
Are you sure you should've
told the Ninja brat

277
00:14:17,774 --> 00:14:19,735
all of that, Lord Ras?

278
00:14:19,735 --> 00:14:21,778
Information can be power.

279
00:14:21,778 --> 00:14:25,157
And information can be poison.

280
00:14:25,157 --> 00:14:27,743
I omitted some of my intentions,

281
00:14:27,743 --> 00:14:30,704
but everything I
told him was true.

282
00:14:30,704 --> 00:14:34,499
And that truth will
poison his mind.

283
00:14:34,499 --> 00:14:38,086
And that poison will
spread to the other Ninja.

284
00:14:38,086 --> 00:14:40,339
And drive them all apart.

285
00:14:40,339 --> 00:14:41,840
Exactly.

286
00:14:41,840 --> 00:14:43,759
Because they are the only threat

287
00:14:43,759 --> 00:14:46,345
to my main goal in
this tournament:

288
00:14:46,345 --> 00:14:50,015
gaining control of all
the Elemental Powers.

289
00:14:50,015 --> 00:14:54,102
That is the only way I can
create the Dragon Icons I need.

290
00:14:54,102 --> 00:14:56,188
Is a Dragon Icon how you lured

291
00:14:56,188 --> 00:14:58,899
and trapped that Source
Dragon under Imperium?

292
00:14:58,899 --> 00:15:01,193
Yes. Without the proper Icons,

293
00:15:01,193 --> 00:15:04,321
summoning Source
Dragons is impossible.

294
00:15:04,321 --> 00:15:06,823
So we cannot suffer
any more losses

295
00:15:06,823 --> 00:15:10,744
at the hands of the Ninja,
like Jay Walker did.

296
00:15:10,744 --> 00:15:14,331
We must win by any
means necessary.

297
00:15:14,331 --> 00:15:16,375
Of course, Master.

298
00:15:19,837 --> 00:15:21,839
And we're back!

299
00:15:21,839 --> 00:15:25,217
Every game, the competition
gets competitiver,

300
00:15:25,217 --> 00:15:30,013
the intensity gets intenser,
and fun gets funner!

301
00:15:30,013 --> 00:15:33,350
And that's not gonna stop
now with our next battle:

302
00:15:33,350 --> 00:15:35,018
You know her, you love her.

303
00:15:35,018 --> 00:15:36,770
Nya!

304
00:15:36,770 --> 00:15:39,731
[crowd cheering]

305
00:15:41,024 --> 00:15:45,529
Versus the mysterious man of
few words and fewer fears.

306
00:15:45,529 --> 00:15:46,572
Nokt!

307
00:15:52,619 --> 00:15:54,746
Where's your brother?

308
00:15:54,746 --> 00:15:56,540
Not here to cheer?

309
00:15:56,540 --> 00:16:01,003
Or what of that
other useless Ninja?

310
00:16:01,003 --> 00:16:04,548
The one you supposedly love?

311
00:16:04,548 --> 00:16:07,050
He's just trying to get
into your head, Nya.

312
00:16:07,050 --> 00:16:10,220
Well I'm gonna get into
his head with my fists!

313
00:16:10,220 --> 00:16:12,639
Wyldfyre, your
anger's not helping.

314
00:16:12,639 --> 00:16:14,725
It's helping me stay angry!

315
00:16:16,935 --> 00:16:21,023
This battle is ramping
up to be legendary!

316
00:16:21,023 --> 00:16:22,149
During this fight, three...

317
00:16:22,149 --> 00:16:24,359
Count 'em, one, two, three.

318
00:16:24,359 --> 00:16:26,820
Holographic gems
will appear randomly.

319
00:16:27,112 --> 00:16:29,781
The goal: whoever
gets the most, wins!

320
00:16:34,786 --> 00:16:37,247
Yeah! Go Nya!

321
00:16:37,247 --> 00:16:39,875
[dramatic music]

322
00:16:40,167 --> 00:16:44,213
[both grunting]

323
00:16:57,100 --> 00:17:00,687
One gem for Nokt, and
a big fat zip for Nya!

324
00:17:00,687 --> 00:17:03,440
But the game's just started!
Anything could happen!

325
00:17:03,440 --> 00:17:07,778
I was expecting the other
member of your family.

326
00:17:08,070 --> 00:17:09,655
You think Kai was tough?

327
00:17:09,655 --> 00:17:12,616
You've never seen
me when I'm mad.

328
00:17:12,616 --> 00:17:16,286
[dramatic music continues]

329
00:17:17,371 --> 00:17:18,747
Hyah!

330
00:17:23,252 --> 00:17:25,504
And just like that,
it's a tie game!

331
00:17:25,504 --> 00:17:26,964
Whoot-Whoot-Stang-the-Zoot!

332
00:17:31,176 --> 00:17:33,178
Get your Rising
Dragon ready, Nya,

333
00:17:33,178 --> 00:17:34,513
he's gonna Shatterspin!

334
00:17:44,565 --> 00:17:48,652
Yes! Destroy him so hard, Nya!

335
00:17:48,652 --> 00:17:50,195
But not angrily.

336
00:17:50,195 --> 00:17:51,864
A friendly destroy.

337
00:17:52,114 --> 00:17:55,617
-[dramatic music continues]
-[both grunting]

338
00:18:10,340 --> 00:18:13,343
[crowd cheering]

339
00:18:15,429 --> 00:18:17,639
And Nokt is victorious!

340
00:18:17,639 --> 00:18:20,184
What an amazing,
incredible battle!

341
00:18:22,186 --> 00:18:25,397
What? But the gem disappeared
right before I was gonna get it!

342
00:18:25,647 --> 00:18:27,941
Sorry! Rules of the game!

343
00:18:41,038 --> 00:18:43,957
Okay, I know this
doesn't look good.

344
00:18:43,957 --> 00:18:46,627
Yeah, it looks super terrible.

345
00:18:46,627 --> 00:18:48,504
-Thanks, Wyldfyre.
-You're welcome.

346
00:18:48,504 --> 00:18:50,839
But Ninja never quit, right?

347
00:18:57,596 --> 00:19:02,809
Up next: Sora, Elemental
Master of Tech and Balance!

348
00:19:02,809 --> 00:19:08,565
Versus Cinder, Elemental
Master of Smoke and now Heat!

349
00:19:13,111 --> 00:19:15,405
[both grunting]

350
00:19:15,405 --> 00:19:19,493
I've been waiting for a rematch
since the Wyldness, girl.

351
00:19:21,954 --> 00:19:24,540
This isn't just a test
of Elemental Skills.

352
00:19:24,831 --> 00:19:26,708
It's a challenge of the mind!

353
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:29,169
The competitors must
solve these puzzles,

354
00:19:29,169 --> 00:19:32,381
including a swing
over a fiery pit!

355
00:19:32,673 --> 00:19:34,091
You were right.

356
00:19:34,091 --> 00:19:36,718
Sora admitted she
used her powers

357
00:19:36,718 --> 00:19:38,804
and let me think
I did it myself.

358
00:19:39,096 --> 00:19:42,015
You'll see I'm right about
a great many things, Arin.

359
00:19:42,307 --> 00:19:44,810
Jay Walker worked at
the Administration.

360
00:19:44,810 --> 00:19:47,771
I think he knows where my
parents disappeared to.

361
00:19:48,063 --> 00:19:52,442
Any information Jay
Walker has, I also have.

362
00:19:52,442 --> 00:19:54,194
[bell dinging]

363
00:19:55,612 --> 00:19:59,116
[both grunting]

364
00:20:01,827 --> 00:20:04,079
Only a few ways
these could work.

365
00:20:17,926 --> 00:20:20,179
You always fall for that trick!

366
00:20:20,179 --> 00:20:22,848
You think I'm not prepared?

367
00:20:24,266 --> 00:20:26,185
[gong ringing]

368
00:20:29,813 --> 00:20:32,274
There are like a gazillion
patterns to this one!

369
00:20:32,274 --> 00:20:33,317
Ugh.

370
00:20:34,651 --> 00:20:36,695
Let's try something simple.

371
00:20:36,695 --> 00:20:38,572
1-1-1-1-1.

372
00:20:43,785 --> 00:20:46,496
-[both grunting]
-[Cinder yells]

373
00:20:47,456 --> 00:20:49,333
Sora wins!

374
00:20:49,333 --> 00:20:51,835
[all cheering]

375
00:21:11,688 --> 00:21:12,731
Huh?

376
00:21:29,581 --> 00:21:31,708
What are you?
Where are you taking me?

377
00:21:31,708 --> 00:21:33,418
There's nothing here.

378
00:21:34,378 --> 00:21:37,256
If I had my powers, I'd
make an earth bridge

379
00:21:37,256 --> 00:21:39,383
and follow you to
whatever is out there...

380
00:21:42,678 --> 00:21:45,013
Another Monastery?

381
00:21:45,013 --> 00:21:47,057
[dramatic closing music]

